meta {
  name: Write a piece (first sync)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/pieces/{{pieceId}}/sync
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "update": "AQrpBwAHAQdkZWZhdWx0AwlwYXJhZ3JhcGgHAOkHAAYEAOkHARVUaGUga2V0dGxlIGNsaWNrcyBvZmaH6QcBAwloYXJkQnJlYWuH6QcXBgQA6QcYGmFuZCBmb3IgYSBzZWNvbmQgdGhlIGhvdXNlh+kHGAMJaGFyZEJyZWFrh+kHMwYEAOkHNA1yZW1lbWJlcnMgeW91KAEEbWV0YQhsYW5ndWFnZQF3AmVuAA==",
    "stateVector": "AA=="
  }
}

docs {
  The piece is created by its first sync, under the id in {{pieceId}}.
  Look at `piece.text` (the API read the words out of the Yjs data) and `piece.language` ("en": the language is in the document too).
  `update` is what the server has that this device does not (empty here).
  To start clean, change pieceId in collection.bru.
  (These requests carry ready-made Yjs data, made by a script, as if a device typed it.)
}
